    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d529-a3">

                <pb facs="0730" n="636" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg636"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 2 to inclosure 1 in No.
                    517.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hyatt to the
                            Commandant.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Santiago
                                de Cuba</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-04-10"><hi rendition="#italic">April 10,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge receipt of
                    your attentive communication of yesterday, advising me that an American citizen,
                    Bert S. Skiller by name, had, in company with others, been taken by the Spanish
                    torpedo boat <hi rendition="#italic">Galicia</hi>, in a small boat, 3 miles from
                    Caleta, and is now confined in the city carcel, subject to your honor’s court,
                    in order to ascertain the purposes of coming to these coasts.</p>
                <p>With such being the statement of facts, and said citizen not having been taken
                    with arms in hand, as I understand, I beg to solicit your honor’s attention to
                    the fact that, in accordance with royal order of May 19, 1877, he should be
                    transferred to the civil jurisdiction for trial, with as little delay as
                    possible, in compliance with the provisions of the protocol between Spain and
                    the United States of America, dated January 12, 1877.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pulaski F. Hyatt</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
